    "lineage",
    "warnings"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Baseline columns describe expected talent/context behavior.",
    "Residual columns describe state evidence versus baseline.",
    "Talent is represented as surfaces and distributions, not a single baseline number.",
    "Player and pitcher props are downstream contracts over shared distributions.",
    "Starter innings and hook behavior are encoded as an exit/workload path distribution, not a single linear trend.",
    "Reliever performance is a first-class individual-arm state surface, not only a team bullpen aggregate.",
    "Reliever availability and first-up routing are separate component distributions before reliever damage is modeled.",
    "Relief-chain outputs must represent likely entry state, workload, inherited-runner damage, and chain-break risk.",
    "For each batting side there is one opponent pitching path: projected starter phase followed by projected reliever-chain phase.",
    "Evidence coverage is required so sparse data cannot masquerade as stable form.",
    "No M2 weights, fixed memory lengths, or hand-tuned conclusions are part of this contract."
  ]
}
